{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":343197,"name":"Tanzir Hasan","username":"Tanzir_Hasan","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/97f17d/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-02-17T15:21:01.468Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI wish to achieve the following: I update my backend code, and bugbot will look at my frontend prs (or even just main) and tell me that I messed something up because the types no longer work as the frontend expects. I don’t have an easy way of doing it with bugbot so I’ve just been resorting to \u003cspan class=\"mention\"\u003e@claude\u003c/span\u003e which is actually quite good for this, but I don’t want to do that all the time. Are there any ways around this?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-02-19T22:01:31.226Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":207,"reads":17,"readers_count":16,"score":1043.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":152120,"topic_slug":"any-way-of-using-multiple-repositories-in-bugbot","display_username":"Tanzir Hasan","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":87691,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/any-way-of-using-multiple-repositories-in-bugbot/152120/1","reactions":[{"id":"heavy_plus_sign","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":344014,"name":"Nvidia RTX Pro 6000","username":"valentinoPereira","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/valentinopereira/{size}/78806_2.png","created_at":"2026-02-19T06:47:08.870Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eNO.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor type failures on different repos, you might be able to \u003ca href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/61889035/how-do-i-use-github-actions-to-checkout-a-different-public-repo-then-add-some-f\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eset it up\u003c/a\u003e on CI github actions. and hack your way there.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInstead I’ll suggest to switch to a monorepo pattern instead of maintaining separate repos. I’ve had my share of separate repos and they have always let me down. More here: \u003ca href=\"https://circleci.com/blog/monorepo-dev-practices/\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eBenefits and challenges of monorepo development practices - CircleCI\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-02-19T06:48:38.952Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":15,"readers_count":14,"score":28.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":152120,"topic_slug":"any-way-of-using-multiple-repositories-in-bugbot","display_username":"Nvidia RTX Pro 6000","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://circleci.com/blog/monorepo-dev-practices/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Benefits and challenges of monorepo development practices - CircleCI","clicks":4},{"url":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/61889035/how-do-i-use-github-actions-to-checkout-a-different-public-repo-then-add-some-f","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":70101,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/any-way-of-using-multiple-repositories-in-bugbot/152120/3","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":344336,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-02-19T17:02:18.648Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, cross-repo context isn’t supported in Bugbot right now. It only reviews PRs within a single repository.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA few workarounds to consider:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMonorepo: If you can move backend and frontend into one repo, Bugbot will naturally see both sides when reviewing changes. This also makes cross-boundary type checks easier with standard CI tools.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTeam Rules: If you’re on a Teams plan, you can set shared Bugbot rules that apply to all connected repos. This won’t enable cross-repo type checking, but it helps enforce consistent standards. See the docs for details: \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/docs/bugbot\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eBugbot | Cursor Docs\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCI-based approach: Set up a GitHub Action that checks out both repos and runs type checking in the PR. The community reply above links to a good pattern for this.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor the specific goal of catching type mismatches between frontend and backend, a monorepo or a CI pipeline will likely work better than Bugbot. Even if cross-repo were supported, static type checking tools are more reliable for catching these issues.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis has come up before, and the team knows there’s interest in cross-repo support. There’s no timeline yet, but your report helps with prioritization.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-02-19T17:02:18.648Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":7,"reads":13,"readers_count":12,"score":52.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":152120,"topic_slug":"any-way-of-using-multiple-repositories-in-bugbot","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://cursor.com/docs/bugbot","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Bugbot | Cursor Docs","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/any-way-of-using-multiple-repositories-in-bugbot/152120/5","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":344408,"name":"Tanzir Hasan","username":"Tanzir_Hasan","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/97f17d/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-02-19T20:20:42.428Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eYeah a monorepo would solve this quite nicely. Unfortunately the codebase is enormous and won’t be made a monorepo any time soon, I haven’t investigated the CI approach but I imagine that is also difficult to implement but regardless both of those are more correct than trying to use bugbot. Thank you both for the response, I’ll try to convince my team to prioritize a monorepo in the next few months.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-02-19T20:21:14.044Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":3,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":11,"readers_count":10,"score":22.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":152120,"topic_slug":"any-way-of-using-multiple-repositories-in-bugbot","display_username":"Tanzir Hasan","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":70101,"username":"valentinoPereira","name":"Nvidia RTX Pro 6000","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/valentinopereira/{size}/78806_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":87691,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/any-way-of-using-multiple-repositories-in-bugbot/152120/6","reactions":[{"id":"+1","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":352190,"name":"Michael Gabriel","username":"shamashel","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/shamashel/{size}/23868_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-05T11:32:43.858Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/deanrie\"\u003e@deanrie\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEchoing the same issue from my team. Is there any particular reason github agentic workflows supports this but bugbot can’t, or is this on the roadmap? If needed, I can have someone from my company communicate this through more official channels\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-03-05T11:51:31.362Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":4,"reads":9,"readers_count":8,"score":26.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":152120,"topic_slug":"any-way-of-using-multiple-repositories-in-bugbot","display_username":"Michael Gabriel","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":22630,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/any-way-of-using-multiple-repositories-in-bugbot/152120/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":357650,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-13T08:44:08.880Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/shamashel\"\u003e@shamashel\u003c/a\u003e, good question. BugBot currently works within a single repository. It only analyzes the PR diff and the code in that repo. GitHub’s Agentic Workflows and similar tools work differently because they spin up a full agent that can clone and navigate multiple repos. BugBot is more focused on the individual PR context, which is a deliberate tradeoff for speed and reliability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere’s no cross-repo support on the roadmap right now, but we’ve noted the interest. I also saw a separate feature request here: \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/multi-repo-bugbot-support/153688\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eMulti-Repo BugBot Support\u003c/a\u003e. That’s helpful for tracking demand.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf your team wants to push this through official channels, that works too. Your account rep or sales contact can pass it along. The more concrete the use case is, like “we need type consistency checks between repos X and Y”, the easier it is to prioritize.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the meantime, a CI-based approach, like checking out both repos in a GitHub Action, is probably the most practical way to catch cross-repo issues automatically.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-03-13T08:44:08.880Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":7,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":17,"reads":8,"readers_count":7,"score":86.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":152120,"topic_slug":"any-way-of-using-multiple-repositories-in-bugbot","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/multi-repo-bugbot-support/153688","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Multi-Repo BugBot Support","clicks":11}],"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":22630,"username":"shamashel","name":"Michael Gabriel","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/shamashel/{size}/23868_2.png"},"bookmark